      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-306392",
      ":question/problem": "A large orchard covers $190$ acres. To estimate the total number of apple trees, an agricultural researcher randomly selects $6$ different $1$-acre plots and counts the trees in each plot. The number of trees in these plots are $43$, $58$, $50$, $62$, $55$, and $47$.\n\nBased on the **mean** of the sample, which of the following ranges contains the best estimate for the number of trees in the entire orchard?"
